---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Subscribe from '~/components/Subscribe.astro';
import { personLd } from '~/lib/jsonld';
import { SITE, SOCIAL, PROJECTS } from '~/site.config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  type="profile"
  description="Katrina Delos Reyes is an engineering leader, writer, and independent researcher studying how AI is changing software engineering and what follows for work, organizations, and people."
  jsonLd={personLd()}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head measure">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>Katrina Delos Reyes</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Engineering leader, builder, and independent writer and researcher. I study what AI is doing to software and
        follow the consequences into organizations, work, education, economics, and institutions.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I’m an engineering leader working at the intersection of software, advanced development, and consequential
        technology. Software engineering is my home base, and it is where I first watch new capabilities meet real
        constraints: deadlines, correctness, safety, accountability, and the people responsible for all of them.
      </p>

      <h2 id="why-software">Why software first</h2>
      <p>
        Software is one of the first fields where AI-produced work is showing up at scale. Code can now be generated,
        tested, reviewed, and explained by machines, often faster than people can check it. That makes software a useful
        early warning system. Questions that will eventually matter everywhere show up here first: what counts as
        evidence, who is accountable, how expertise forms, and what a team is for.
      </p>

      <h2 id="the-investigation">The investigation</h2>
      <p>
        I call the broader body of work <a href="/">{SITE.investigation}</a>: an ongoing investigation into AI, software,
        work, and what happens to humans when intelligence becomes abundant. It takes four forms:{' '}
        <a href="/essays">Essays</a> make long-form arguments. <a href="/research">Research</a> asks specific questions
        and shows its methods. <a href="/observatory">The Observatory</a> tracks signals of change.{' '}
        <a href="/notes">Field Notes</a> hold what isn’t settled yet.
      </p>
      <p>
        I try to work in the open, with my uncertainty visible. When I have a hypothesis, I call it one. When the evidence
        changes, the writing gets updated and dated.
      </p>

      <h2 id="principles">How I approach the work</h2>
      <blockquote>
        <p>My work gives me the questions. Public evidence gives me the material.</p>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        My professional experience shapes which questions seem important. It does not supply the evidence. Nothing here
        discloses or relies on confidential employer information: no internal metrics, programs, customers, architectures,
        or anecdotes, anonymized or not. Public arguments have to stand on public evidence.
      </p>
      <p>The test I hold myself to:</p>
      <p class="test">
        Could an intelligent outsider reconstruct the factual basis of this argument using the sources provided?
      </p>
      <p>Views here are my own and do not represent any employer.</p>

      <h2 id="background">Background</h2>
      <p>
        I studied computer science and mathematics at the University of Maryland, College Park. Since then I’ve worked as a
        software and systems engineer and moved into engineering leadership, mostly in environments where software has to
        be right: DevSecOps, agile transformation, and advanced development for high-consequence systems.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="section building" id="building" aria-labelledby="building-heading">
      <h2 id="building-heading">I build things, too.</h2>
      <p class="intro">Outside engineering and research, I build and run a few things in technology, community, and weddings.</p>
      <dl>
        {
          PROJECTS.map((p) => (
            <div>
              <dt>{p.url ? <a href={p.url}>{p.name}</a> : p.name}</dt>
              <dd>{p.description}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="section contact" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
      <h2 id="contact-heading">Elsewhere</h2>
      <ul class="sans">
        <li><a href={SOCIAL.github} rel="me">GitHub</a></li>
        <li><a href={SOCIAL.linkedin} rel="me">LinkedIn</a></li>
        <li><a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></li>
        <li><a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="fine sans">
        For wedding planning and coordination, please contact{' '}
        <a href="https://kmaeweddings.com">K. Mae Weddings</a>{' '}directly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <Subscribe id="about-subscribe" />
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .test {
    font-style: italic;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
  }

  .building,
  .contact {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .building h2,
  .contact h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .intro {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
  }

  dl {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  dt {
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .contact ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .fine {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.84rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
</style>
